$change_voice — RVC voice conversion on sounds[]



SUMMARY

  Converts each sound in sounds[] using Retrieval-based Voice Conversion (RVC)
  via rvc-python. Typical use: change vocals after $music_separation(model=2stem).



SYNTAX

  $change_voice
  $change_voice(model=MuscleMan, f0up_key=2, protect=0.5)
  $change_voice(model=@voices)   — one output per model from @voices texts[] ($list)
  $change_voice(model_path='models/rvc/MuscleMan/muscleman.pth', index_path='...')



INPUT

  sounds[] — required; WAV/MP3 vocal tracks.



OUTPUT

  sounds[] — one converted WAV per input sound per model.



ARGUMENTS

  model= — subdirectory under models/rvc/ (default MuscleMan), or model=@ref for several.

  model_path= / index_path= — explicit .pth and .index files.

  device= — cuda:0 or cpu:0 (auto-detect GPU if omitted).

  version= — v1, v2, or omit for auto-detect from .pth (default: auto).

  f0up_key= — pitch shift in semitones (default 0).

  protect= — consonant protection 0–0.5 (default 0.33).

  index_rate= — index blend rate (default 0.5).

  f0method= — pitch extractor: harvest, pm, crepe, rmvpe, …



MODELS

  models/rvc/MuscleMan/muscleman.pth
  models/rvc/MuscleMan/added_IVF231_Flat_nprobe_1_MuscleMan_v2.index

TRAINING CHECKPOINTS

  Classic RVC G_*.pth under models/rvc/<name>/ are auto-converted to <name>_inference.pth.
  Applio / non-standard training (config.json + G_ only) cannot be converted here —
  use the trainer’s “Extract small model” export and place the resulting .pth in the folder.

REQUIREMENTS

  rvc-python in .venvs/change_voice (Python 3.10; isolated from media stack).
  Setup: powershell -File tools\setup_external_venvs.ps1



ENVIRONMENT

  AH_EMULATE_CHANGE_VOICE=1 — stub WAV text files without rvc-python.
  AH_CHANGE_VOICE_AUTO_CONVERT=0 — skip automatic G_*.pth conversion.



EXAMPLE

  @vocals: @track -> $music_separation(model=2stem)
  @mm: @vocals -> $change_voice(model=MuscleMan, f0up_key=2, protect=0.5)



PROMPT-CONSUMING

  No.
